     "text": "calumny, devotion to the Trident-holder ( S'iva ), strength",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "to restrain the self, and freedom from the contact of wicked",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 4,
     "text": "men.",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  "r3": {
   "type": "translated_stanza",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "63. Fortitude in adversity, forgiveness in prosperity,",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "cleverness of speech in an assembly, valour in war, a liking",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "( earnest desire ) for fame, and untiring application to the",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 4,
     "text": "study of the Vedas—all these are natural with the magnani-",
     "end": "hyphen"
    },
    {
     "n": 5,
     "text": "",
     "end": "join"
    },
    {
     "n": 6,
     "text": "mous.",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  "r4": {
   "type": "translated_stanza",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "64. Who taught this course of conduct, difficult like lying",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "on the edge of a sword-blade, to the good, viz. charity well",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "concealed, quick reception to him who comes to their house,",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 4,
     "text": "silence after doing good, not announcing in public their",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 5,
     "text": "kindness ( to others ), freedom from arrogance in prosperity,",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 6,
     "text": "and speaking of others in terms free from disrespectfulness.",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  "r5": {
   "type": "translated_stanza",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "65. Laudable charity for the hand, submission at the",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "feet of elders for the head, true words for the mouth, in-",
     "end": "hyphen"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "",
     "end": "join"
    },
    {
     "n": 4,
     "text": "comparable valour for victorious arms, a quiescent state",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 5,
     "text": "for the heart, Vedic knowledge (acquired by the ears) for",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 6,
     "text": "",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 7,
     "text": "the ears; of high-souled person these are the ornaments",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 8,
     "text": "even though they have no wealth.",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  "r6": {
   "type": "translated_stanza",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "66. In prosperity the mind of magnanimous men becomes",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "tender like a lotus, while in adversity it becomes hard as a",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 4,
     "text": "solid rock:",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  "r7": {
   "type": "translated_stanza",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "67. Not the least trace of water is to be found when it",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "falls ( lit. stands ) upon heated iron; the same, lying on a",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "lotus-leaf, shines assuming the form of pearls; it is trans-",
     "end": "hyphen"
    },
    {
     "n": 4,
     "text": "formed into a pearl when it falls into the cavity of the shells",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 5,
     "text": "in the sea while (the sun is) in conjunction with the con-",
     "end": "hyphen"
    },
    {
     "n": 6,
     "text": "stellation Svâti. In general, the lowest, the mediocre, and",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 7,
     "text": "the highest degree of excellence is imparted ( to a thing )",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 8,
     "text": "by association.",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
